[h1]OpenZone Research[/h1]
Research points and a technology tree for OpenZone servers. Samples are processed at stations into data and point carriers, carriers are handed in at a faction terminal, and the faction's pool is spent on its own tree, instantly or as a timed project. Every chain, point type, station and tree node is the administrator's JSON. Part of the OpenZone series, built for the [UA] STALKER: Zone Protocol server.

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Stations: put the input into a station's cargo and press F; the station takes the input at once, works by the clock (a restart does not lose the work), puts the result into its own cargo and keeps going while input is left.
[*]Rules in JSON: which device takes what, how long, what comes out and with what chance; purity carried by samples and multiplied by modules in the station's slots.
[*]Carriers and data: a carrier hides its value until identified at a terminal; handing it in pays the pool of the faction of the one who hands it in.
[*]The tree: branches per faction, nodes with a cost in points and materials, instant nodes and timed projects, parents by "all" or "any"; the leader or the holder of the research post spends.
[*]Factions from the core: the player's organisation, else the base faction, with the faction's name and colour on the tree screen.
[*]Static stations placed from JSON once and remembered, an example types.xml, two example packs.
[*]Administration in the OpenZone admin window (VPP): the nine configs in the CONFIG pane, the RESEARCH pane for pools, resets, grants and reloads.
[/list]
[b]Requires[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1559212036]Community Framework[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798432022]OpenZone Core[/url]. Factions come from [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798436325]OpenZone Factions[/url]; without it every player belongs to the default owner from the settings.
[b]Coming from ZP_Research[/b] This is its successor on the OpenZone core: the same game rules, new code. Nothing carries over from a ZP_Research server; the mod starts empty and ships a converter for the ZP example packs.
[b]Companion[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3804762616]OpenZone Research VPP[/url] (the RESEARCH pane of the admin window).
[b]Source code[/b] [url=https://github.com/covalschi/openzone-research]github.com/covalschi/openzone-research[/url]

[b]Licence, repacking, selling[/b]
You may repack this mod into your server's own pack, keeping the attribution and the same licence. You may not sell it, sublicense it or include it in any paid bundle. Running it on a server that accepts donations, sells cosmetics or priority queue slots is fine. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with the additional permission in NOTICE.

